# BlockVote environment files
#
# LOCAL (this machine):
#   .env.development  → source of truth for Hardhat + local Mongo + localhost:3000
#   .env              → active copy used by Next.js / Hardhat local (gitignored)
#
# PRODUCTION (live site):
#   Vercel project env  → real source of truth for https://www.devz.co.in
#   .env.production     → optional LOCAL ARCHIVE only (Sepolia deploy keys / contract addrs)
#                         Never activated into .env. Never used by next dev.
#
# Commands (from Voting/):
#   yarn env:init     # create .env.development (+ optional .env.production archive)
#   yarn env:dev      # activate local profile
#   yarn env:status
#   yarn deploy:sepolia  # reads .env.production for wallets only; does not switch local .env
#
# Templates:
#   .env.development.example
#   .env.production.example
#
# Android:
#   local flavor → http://10.0.2.2:3000/
#   prod flavor  → https://www.devz.co.in/  (talks to Vercel-backed API)
#
# Voter surfaces:
#   Android app      → remote voting with 360° surrounding scan; first vote + one change
#   Polling station  → {APP_URL}/station (admin activates the PC) → {APP_URL}/station/vote
#                      web ballot, no surrounding scan, vote is FINAL and overrides app votes
#   Invite           → {APP_URL}/org/{admin}/election/{title}/{electionId} (opens the app on phones)
#
# Optional voting rules (defaults shown):
#   VOTING_OPEN_TIME=07:00
#   VOTING_CLOSE_TIME=18:00
#   VOTING_TIMEZONE=Asia/Kolkata
#   STATION_SESSION_SECRET=   # falls back to JWT_SECRET
#   ADMIN_API_KEY=            # required for server-to-server POST /api/relay/vote
